8	// Search & social metadata, visible and editable WITHOUT paying for a build.
9	//
10	// Where these values actually live: there is no seo column anywhere. The head
11	// of the project's own `index.html` IS the storage (see lib/foundation.ts for
12	// the scaffold the agent is handed, and the head-writing instructions in the
13	// SYSTEM prompt in lib/agent.ts). So this panel reads the draft SOURCE
14	// index.html the editor already holds, and a save has to rewrite that same
15	// file — which is why the endpoint contract below is what it is.
16	//
17	// Three separate copies of index.html exist per project, and they are NOT
18	// interchangeable:
19	//   draft  + kind "source"  — what the agent edits and what this panel reads.
20	//   draft  + kind "build"   — the compiled output the in-editor preview serves.
21	//   published + kind "build" — what visitors get; only the publish route writes it.
22	// A save must touch the first two and must never touch the third: going live
23	// stays an explicit act. That is stated again on the endpoint contract below.
24	//
25	// What lib/site-seo.ts does on top of this, at serve time and for published
26	// sites only, is a BACKSTOP for gaps — it never overrides a value that is
27	// present. The "What visitors see" column mirrors those rules exactly so the
28	// panel can never show something different from what is actually served.
29	
30	/** lib/site-seo.ts's own placeholder constant. Not exported there; mirrored. */
31	const PLACEHOLDER_TITLE = "Kodely Site";
32	
33	// Guidance, not limits. Straight out of the SYSTEM prompt the builder is given
34	// (lib/agent.ts): title under ~60 characters, description ~150. Going over is
35	// allowed — search engines truncate, they do not reject — so this only ever
36	// changes a colour and a number, never disables the save.
37	const TITLE_TARGET = 60;
38	const DESC_TARGET = 150;
